{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Then you shall investigate and inquire and search thoroughly</b> — the investigation and inquiry are explained in the words of our Sages (Sanhedrin 40a). Scripture mentioned this in the case of the seduced city and in the case of one who serves idolatry, but it did not mention it thus in the case of the false prophet and the inciter, because the prophet makes himself publicly known through his signs and wonders, and concerning the inciter Scripture speaks with the enticed person <b>for you shall surely kill him</b>, and he is one who knows and testifies, as it says <b>and you shall not spare and you shall not conceal him</b>. But in the case of the seduced city and one who serves idolatry, which are matters that reach us by hearsay, Scripture mentioned investigation and inquiry concerning them. And there was no need to mention it thus in the case of other capital offenders, for by a fortiori reasoning the matter is known. And it says concerning conspiring witnesses (Deuteronomy 19:18), <b>and the judges shall investigate thoroughly</b>, because it is not known which of the two parties is telling the truth except after extensive inquiry. And with respect to the law, all of them derive this one from that one by means of a gezerah shavah, and from all of them there emerged for us seven inquiries and examinations:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:49:41.046381453Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}